tested; ADF activity in 2026 is in Haut-Uele/Ituri, far to the south-east.","unit":"CD5209-bambesa","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","source_ids":[44,46,63]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"medium","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Main towns: Dingila (GRID3 'Gbaka', Bambili HA) and Bambesa territory centre (GRID3 'Embite', Bambesa HA)","evidence":"Territorial seat and main trading town under state administration; no armed-group activity reported in Bambesa territory in 2025-2026 searches. Bas-Uele FARDC deployment described as thin, so the PNC is assumed to be the main day-to-day security force.","unit":"CD5209-bambesa","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[44,62]}],"sources":{"44":{"url":"https://actualite.cd/2026/03/08/agression-rwandaise-obed-mutuale-appelle-renforcer-les-fardc-dans-le-bas-uele-et-equiper","title":"Agression rwandaise: Obed Mutuale appelle a renforcer les FARDC dans le Bas-Uele","publisher":"Actualite.cd","date":"2026-03-08"},"46":{"url":"https://fr.allafrica.com/stories/202607140342.html","title":"Haut-Uele - La progression des ADF provoque le déplacement de plus de 10 000 civils vers Watsa et Wamba","publisher":"Radio Okapi via AllAfrica","date":"2026-07-14"},"63":{"url":"https://monusco.unmissions.org/en/node/9033","title":"MONUSCO note on Bas-Uele Mbororo herders issue","publisher":"MONUSCO","date":"2016-05"},"62":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bambesa_Territory","title":"Bambesa Territory","publisher":"Wikipedia"}},"units":{"CD5209-bambesa":"Bambesa territory (Bas-Uele) lies far from the active conflict zones of eastern DRC and no armed group is reported to hold or contest territory there in 2025-2026. Recent regional security reporting concerns ADF incursions into Haut-Uele (Wamba, Watsa) and Ituri, several hundred km to the south-east, not Bambesa. Historical insecurity (LRA in the late 2000s, Mbororo herder tensions, poaching around Bili-Uele) has not translated into armed-group control. The main towns Dingila (GRID3 'Gbaka') and Bambesa centre (GRID3 'Embite') are administered and policed by the state; rural villages are assigned to the PNC by default state presence."}}